log, /tmp/rayzor-abstract-statics-fmt-v4-check.log, and /tmp/rayzor-abstract-statics-clippy-v4.log. cargo fmt --all -- --check and cargo clippy --workspace --all-features --all-targets -- -D warnings both exit successfully.\n\nThe first prototype repaired storage but did not execute direct static data-field calls. MIR showed method placeholders whose calls and surrounding assertions were dropped; separate side-effect checks caught that. After call lowering was repaired, the import inline-value exporter still substituted a mutable abstract counter into same-named fields. Correcting its mutability filter made the complete reproducer pass.","files":null}]}